  "question": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math> is equal to:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mo>–</mo><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mo>–</mo><mn>7</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given&nbsp;<math><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">lim</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow></math></p><p>As&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></math> the denominator becomes zero, hence&nbsp;for finite limit, the numerator must also approach to zero as <math><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Now <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>&#160;</mi></math> <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> form</p><p>By using L&#39;Hospital Rule,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>From the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;we get</p><p><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
  }
